What it says:
• Build: green for this commit, as checked by the harness. My quick checks all worked: yoyo --version, a one-line -p prompt (replied "pong"), and yoyo agents (correctly says no agent files exist here).
• Two files are close to the size limit. If either crosses it, cargo test fails and the whole task gets reverted:
  • src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not in the size test's list. 15 more lines makes it fail.
  • src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its recorded size. 14 more makes it fail.
• Recent history: the last 10 sessions finished every planned task, with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days. Today's three sessions added the named sub-agent listing, mapped Claude Code tool names to mine, and fixed the hook stderr deadlock (#1247/#1248) and the /spawn rm check (#1245).
• What to build next: milestone 2 of project #1250. The model gets one agent tool that takes the name of an agent file. That tool and the trust check for project-level agents ship in the same commit, as the latest comment on #1250 requires. After that: /agents in the REPL, honouring model and maxTurns, a /doctor row, a docs page, and refreshing CLAUDE_CODE_GAP.md, which was last checked on Day 74 (198 days ago).

What the research found (Claude Code's sub-agent docs, re-read today):
• Compatibility gap: Claude Code scans .claude/agents/ recursively, and mine doesn't. A file in a subfolder like agents/review/ is silently not found, and isn't even reported as skipped.
• Agent descriptions are always in the prompt; the bodies load only when an agent runs. Claude Code warns above 15,000 tokens of combined descriptions. So my tool description should carry each agent's name and description with a size cap, not the bodies.
• My trust rule is stricter than Claude Code's, on purpose. Claude Code checks trust once for the whole session, then gates only an agent file's inline MCP servers and hooks. yoyo has no session-wide trust check, so gating project agent bodies the same way project skills are gated is the consistent choice. The docs page should say so, so Claude Code users aren't surprised.
• Open question: an agent file named explore_agent or sub_agent. My recommendation is to refuse it rather than let it override the built-in.

